================================================================================
9. VERDICT
================================================================================
PASS.

The opus does what it claims. A browser can write; W-024's answer button works end
to end against a served build, verified by me from a dist removed and rebuilt; the
origin tuple is exact under 17 live probes including three the brief never named;
W-016 behaviour 5 is intact by direct test, not by assertion; the suite bites under
all eleven mutations the brief names. Reds are red-first by cryptographic tree
identity rather than by clock.

The three findings are advisory. F-3 is not this opus's and belongs to a new one.
F-1 and F-2 are both "the artifact is right, its stated justification is not" —
worth a follow-up, not worth another review round: fixing either changes no
behaviour this opus is responsible for, and holding the branch would cost more than
it buys.

For the retro: two process items, not code — the pre-review dispatch that permitted
a bookkeeping-writing verb, and the red-ordering check rule proposed under
disclosure 2, which should be a petitio rather than a fourth prose ruling.
